[StringTable.Subtitle_01]
Listen up! You are to climb Hill 320 and reconnoiter.
[StringTable.Subtitle_02]
Yes, sir.
[StringTable.Subtitle_03]
The seven panzers are advancing along the road.
[StringTable.Subtitle_04]
Quickly lay anti-tank mines at the southern edge of the bridge! 
[StringTable.Subtitle_05]
Yes, sir.
[Submission1.Objectives]
Stop enemy tanks from moving south.
[Submission1.Description]
On the move since shortly after the Germans hit the U.S. front line, your platoon has now reached the foot of Hill 330, just south of a steep-sided stream winding through the dense forest. During your frustrating and confusing journey, you were bounced between headquarters and command posts – no one in authority seemed to know what was going on or what they needed you to do. Finally, about two hours ago, your company commander issued a clear mission: stop any German tanks from moving south via the bridge spanning the stream running between Hills 320 and 330.

Your order:
- stop enemy tanks from moving south.
[Submission1.Success]
Mission accomplished. 
[Submission1.Failed]
Mission failed.